{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WRFChemMetState",
    "description": "What WRF-Chem's chemistry is told about the meteorology of a column: the part of chem_driver's preparation that chem_opt = 170 reads, transcribed from WRF v4.8.0. Three routines. (1) chem_prep (chem/module_chem_utilities.F:8-181), the temperature, pressure and density every chemistry process reads: t_phy = (t + t0) (p/p1000mb)^rcp, p_phy = p + pb, rho = 1/alt. (2) The generated KPP interface (chem/module_kpp_cbmz_mosaic_interface.F:229-241): the third body C_M = FIX(indf_M) = dens2con_a rho and the water FIX(indf_H2O) = dens2con_w qv rho, number densities in molec/cm^3. (3) wesely_driver's near-surface state (chem/module_dep_simple.F:213-235): rhchem = max(5, min(100, 100 qv_1 / (3.80 exp(17.27 (T_1 - 273)/(T_1 - 36)) / pa))) with pa = 0.01 p_1 in hPa, the dew flag rhchem >= 95, and the rain flag qr_1 > 1e-18 or raincv > 0.\n\nTHE TEMPERATURE IS FORMED FROM THE MOIST POTENTIAL TEMPERATURE (FORTRAN_BUGS B34). chem_driver hands chem_prep grid%t_2, which under use_theta_m = 1 -- WRF's default since 4.0, and this run's -- holds theta_m - t0 with theta_m = theta (1 + (R_v/R_d) q_v), not the dry theta - t0 chem_prep's formula assumes. So every chemistry process runs at T (1 + 1.608 q_v): 7.3 K too warm in the moist boundary layer of the chem170 column at step 364 (verified against the cbmz_kpp dump: KPP's TEMP is theta_m * exner to 1.2e-7, and dry theta * exner is 2.3e-2 away). The input here is what chem_prep reads, `theta_m`; `chem_theta_is_moist` = 1 reproduces WRF, and 0 divides out the vapour factor, the formula's intent.\n\nTHE DENSITY IS WHATEVER `alt` HOLDS. chem_prep takes rho = 1/alt with the (1 + qv) factor commented out, the inverse DRY density. The input `alt` is that array; which time level it holds is the mounting document's business (couplings/eqatmchem_scm.esm, FORTRAN_BUGS N128: at chem time WRF's alt is a stale stage of the step, not the one its p and geopotential are).\n\nWHAT IS NOT HERE. chem_prep's u_phy/v_phy, p8w/t8w and its own rh (none read by the chem_opt = 170 processes of this column), and every surface field the chemistry takes directly from the land and surface-layer schemes (tsk, ust, znt, rmol, gsw), which are passed through by the mounting document. MOSAIC's own view of the cell (cairclm, ptotclm, relhumclm, the 233 K floor) is mapaer_tofrom_host's, components/aerosol/mosaic/mosaic_host_mapping.esm, which reads this component's T and rho.\n\nTESTS. Four steps of the chem170 full-chemistry column with the meteorology hooks and a one-minute history (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_full_met.sh; fork ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170 @ 57535398, real32): the inputs are the wrfout frame of the step (the state after the step, which is what chem_driver sees: p_phy reproduces bit for bit) and the emissions dump's alt; the expectations are the cbmz_kpp dump's temp, rho_phy, c_m and fix and the wesely dump's rhchem and flags. WRF forms all of them in real32 and this component in real64, so rel 1e-6; the flags are pinned exactly. Filled by tools/fill_chem_met_state_tests.py.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "license": "MIT",
    "created": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "chem_prep",
      "kpp-interface",
      "wesely",
      "chem_opt-170",
      "column",
      "stage-3"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "WRF-Chem v4.8.0, chem/module_chem_utilities.F (chem_prep), chem/module_kpp_cbmz_mosaic_interface.F (generated KPP interface), chem/module_dep_simple.F (wesely_driver)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Mass layers of the column, WRF kte. A consumer binds its own at the mount edge."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "lev": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NLEV"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "WRFChemMetState": {
      "subsystems": {
        "wrf": {
          "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "theta_m": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "default": 300.0,
          "description": "What chem_prep reads as its potential temperature, grid%t_2 + t0: the MOIST potential temperature theta (1 + (R_v/R_d) q_v) under use_theta_m = 1 (FORTRAN_BUGS B34)."
        },
        "p": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "default": 100000.0,
          "description": "Pressure p + pb (chem_prep's p_phy)."
        },
        "alt": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m^3/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "default": 0.85,
          "description": "Inverse dry density, grid%alt as chem_driver finds it."
        },
        "qv": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Water vapour mixing ratio moist(p_qv)."
        },
        "qr": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Rain water mixing ratio moist(p_qr) (only the lowest layer is read, by wesely_driver's rain flag)."
        },
        "raincv": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^2",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Convective rain over the step (grid%raincv_b); 0 with cu_physics = 0."
        },
        "chem_theta_is_moist": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "1: chem_prep's temperature from theta_m as WRF v4.8.0 does under use_theta_m = 1 (FORTRAN_BUGS B34); 0: from the dry theta_m/(1 + (R_v/R_d) q_v)."
        },
        "pa_per_hpa": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "Pa/hPa",
          "default": 100.0,
          "description": "wesely_driver's pa = .01 p_phy(kts): Pa per hPa."
        },
        "qsat_coef": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "hPa",
          "default": 3.8,
          "description": "The 3.80 of wesely_driver's saturation mixing ratio 3.80 exp(17.27 (T - 273)/(T - 36))/pa (Tetens-type, in g/kg x 1e-3 at pa in hPa)."
        },
        "qsat_a": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 17.27,
          "description": "The 17.27 of wesely_driver's saturation expression."
        },
        "qsat_t1": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 273.0,
          "description": "The 273. of wesely_driver's saturation expression."
        },
        "qsat_t2": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 36.0,
          "description": "The 36. of wesely_driver's saturation expression."
        },
        "pct": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 100.0,
          "description": "Percent per unit relative humidity."
        },
        "rh_min": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 5.0,
          "description": "Lower clamp of rhchem, percent."
        },
        "rh_max": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 100.0,
          "description": "Upper clamp of rhchem, percent."
        },
        "rh_dew": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 95.0,
          "description": "rhchem at or above which wesely_driver sets the dew flag, percent."
        },
        "qr_rain": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "default": 1e-18,
          "description": "Lowest-layer rain water above which wesely_driver sets the rain flag."
        },
        "exner": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "(p_phy/p1000mb)^rcp, chem_prep's Exner function."
        },
        "theta": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The potential temperature chem_prep converts: theta_m itself under B34, or the dry theta."
        },
        "T": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "t_phy, the temperature every chemistry process of the column reads (KPP's TEMP, mapaer_tofrom_host's t_phy)."
        },
        "rho": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "rho_phy = 1/alt."
        },
        "M_air": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "molec/cm^3",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "KPP's third body C_M = FIX(indf_M) = dens2con_a rho_phy."
        },
        "H2O": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "molec/cm^3",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "KPP's fixed water FIX(indf_H2O) = dens2con_w qv rho_phy."
        },
        "pa": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "hPa",
          "description": "Lowest-layer pressure in hPa, wesely_driver's pa."
        },
        "qsat_1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "wesely_driver's saturation mixing ratio of the lowest layer, 3.80 exp(17.27 (T_1 - 273)/(T_1 - 36))/pa."
        },
        "rhchem": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "wesely_driver's near-surface relative humidity in percent, 100 qv_1/qsat_1 held to [5, 100]."
        },
        "wetflag": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when rhchem >= 95 (dew), else 0."
        },
        "rainflag": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when the lowest layer holds rain (qr_1 > 1e-18) or it rained convectively this step, else 0."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "exner",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "^",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  "p",
                  "wrf.p1000mb"
                ]
              },
              "wrf.rcp"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "theta",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": ">",
                "args": [
                  "chem_theta_is_moist",
                  0.5
                ]
              },
              "theta_m",
              {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  "theta_m",
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      1,
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          "wrf.rvovrd",
                          "qv"
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "T",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "theta",
              "exner"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "rho",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "alt"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "M_air",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "wrf.dens2con_a",
              "rho"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "H2O",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "wrf.dens2con_w",
              "qv",
              "rho"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "pa",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "index",
                "args": [
                  "p",
                  1
                ]
              },
              "pa_per_hpa"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "qsat_1",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "qsat_coef",
                  {
                    "op": "exp",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "/",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "*",
                            "args": [
                              "qsat_a",
                              {
                                "op": "-",
                                "args": [
                                  {
                                    "op": "index",
                                    "args": [
                                      "T",
                                      1
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "qsat_t1"
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "op": "-",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "index",
                                "args": [
                                  "T",
                                  1
                                ]
                              },
                              "qsat_t2"
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "pa"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "rhchem",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "max",
            "args": [
              "rh_min",
              {
                "op": "min",
                "args": [
                  "rh_max",
                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          "pct",
                          {
                            "op": "index",
                            "args": [
                              "qv",
                              1
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      "qsat_1"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "wetflag",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": ">=",
                "args": [
                  "rhchem",
                  "rh_dew"
                ]
              },
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "rainflag",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "or",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": ">",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "index",
                        "args": [
                          "qr",
                          1
                        ]
                      },
                      "qr_rain"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": ">",
                    "args": [
                      "raincv",
                      0
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
